      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_separator_search_is_length_bounded",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "The parser looks for `\"\\n\\n\"` with `strstr` even though the remaining input is a bounded byte span, not a NUL-terminated C string. This ignores `buffer_end` and allows the search to read past the heap buffer when the separator is missing. The fix replaces this with `git__memmem(buffer, buffer_end - buffer, \"\\n\\n\", 2)`."
    },
